# Budget Flow API

Node.js Express API (CommonJS) with PostgreSQL (`pg`), Passport Google OAuth, and JWT auth.

## Structure

- `src/app.js` — app entry, middleware, route mounting
- `src/db.js` — shared `pg` Pool
- `src/config/` — Passport and other config
- `src/routes/` — Express routers (`*.js` or `*.routes.js`)

## Conventions

- Use CommonJS (`require` / `module.exports`), not ESM
- Mount routes in `app.js` under clear prefixes (`/auth`, `/api/...`)
- Use parameterized SQL (`$1`, `$2`, ...) — never string-concatenate user input
- Prefer `async/await` with try/catch; return JSON errors with appropriate status codes
- Keep secrets in `.env` (`JWT_*`, `DB_*`, `FRONTEND_URL`, `PORT`) — never commit them
- Match existing style: Express routers, `pool.query` / `db.query`, JWT access + refresh tokens

## Responses

All API responses use a shared shape via `src/utils/response.js`:

```json
{ "status": 200, "message": "...", "data": ... }
```

Default status codes:
- `200` — list, get, update, delete success
- `201` — create success
- `400` — validation / bad request
- `401` — unauthorized
- `403` — forbidden
- `404` — not found
- `409` — conflict (e.g. duplicate)
- `500` — server error

